  message: "Hand-corrected strip on saturation-bounded inconclusive verdict per process-validation-queue-with-bakeoffs-and-uat.md Phase 6.\n\nUAT round-03 of hg-uat-v5.0.1 (~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/bakeoff_artifacts/hg-uat-v5.0.1/lab-notebook/round-03-chatwoot/) returned literal verdict 'inconclusive' because the plan's quantitative thresholds (≥10 csv.erb edges, ≥5/8 ground-truth, +8…+14 baseline delta) were calibrated against a v4.1.0-era chatwoot snapshot (~11 .csv.erb files / 8 ReportsController CSV actions). The current chatwoot working tree (HEAD 8b230c6) contains 6 .csv.erb files / 5 CSV actions — fewer total available targets than the pre-committed thresholds.\n\nMechanism observably moved: 5 .csv.erb renders edges (vs 0 in v4.1.0 baseline). Every app/views/api/v2/accounts/reports/*.csv.erb in the OSS chatwoot tree is bound to its corresponding controller action; plus Api::V1::Accounts::CsatSurveyResponsesController#download. Ground-truth: 4/4 corpus-resident ReportsController CSV actions linked correctly (the 5th, conversation_traffic, points to a missing view file in chatwoot itself — unrelated to hypergumbo). Edge metadata names the binding mechanism explicitly (evidence_type: 'naming_convention', detection_pattern: 'implicit_convention').\n\nStrip rationale: 100% recall on every corpus-resident target. The 'inconclusive' is plurality-shaped exactly like the cohort-path saturation-bounded niche-claim case the playbook §Phase 6 prescribes hand-correction for. The PR #3587 fix is observably effective; the corpus drifted, not the implementation.\n\nOne enterprise/app/views/ implicit-convention gap surfaced separately as DQ-01 (filing pending). See master-report §3.3 + §6.1."  # 8cff
